AI and LLM

- A configurable LLM provider interface.
- Support an external model API or a compatible open-weight model.
- Hugging Face Transformers may be used for self-hosted models.
- Use structured outputs and schema validation.
- The application must continue to support ordinary data processing when the LLM provider is unavailable.

Never hardcode API keys. Use environment variables and server-side secrets.

Background processing and monitoring

- Use a background job system for expensive dataset processing.
- Redis and Celery, or an equivalent queue, may be used when required.
- Use Server-Sent Events (SSE) or WebSockets for live processing logs.
- Use structured backend logging and persistent job states.

